WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.739 --> 00:00:05.762
The room gets quiet, and suddenly your mind gets busy.

2
00:00:05.762 --> 00:00:09.721
You remember tomorrow’s appointment. An unfinished task. A conversation you

3
00:00:09.721 --> 00:00:11.304
wish had gone differently.

4
00:00:11.304 --> 00:00:14.612
With fewer distractions, worries can become more noticeable.

5
00:00:14.977 --> 00:00:20.334
If this happens to you, consider setting aside a brief moment earlier in the

6
00:00:20.334 --> 00:00:23.012
evening to write down what needs attention.

7
00:00:23.012 --> 00:00:26.627
Keep it simple: ‘Check the appointment time tomorrow.’

8
00:00:26.627 --> 00:00:32.652
For a practical concern, you might add one next step and when you’ll take it.

9
00:00:33.017 --> 00:00:38.374
You don’t need a detailed review of everything that could go wrong.

10
00:00:38.374 --> 00:00:43.302
Later, if the same reminder appears in bed, you can gently acknowledge it:

11
00:00:43.302 --> 00:00:47.471
‘I’ve made a note. There’s a time to return to this.’

12
00:00:47.837 --> 00:00:52.581
That doesn’t mean the thought will disappear. You’re giving yourself an option

13
00:00:52.581 --> 00:00:54.558
besides repeatedly working through it.

14
00:00:54.558 --> 00:00:59.897
If writing makes you more alert, skip it or try it earlier.

15
00:00:59.897 --> 00:01:04.306
And you don’t have to demand a completely empty mind before resting.

16
00:01:04.671 --> 00:01:09.466
If worries or sleep difficulties keep affecting your daily life, consider

17
00:01:09.466 --> 00:01:11.645
speaking with a healthcare professional.

18
00:01:11.645 --> 00:01:16.315
For tonight, see whether one concern can wait for a more useful time.
